    "details": "<p><strong>About the Hackathon:</strong></p>\n<p>Edge AI Hackathon 2026 is a national-level hardware innovation challenge organized by the IEEE EDS Student Branch Chapter, IEEE Council on Electronics Design &amp; Automation PMEC. The hackathon aims to encourage students to design and implement real-time Edge AI and Embedded Systems solutions using FPGA, Raspberry Pi, Renesas, ESP32, and Arduino platforms.</p>\n<p>Participants will solve real-world engineering challenges while showcasing innovation, technical excellence, and hardware implementation skills.</p>\n<p><strong>Prize Pool:</strong> ₹45,000</p>\n<p><strong>Eligibility:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Open to B.Tech, M.Tech, and Ph.D. students.</li>\n<li>Team size: 3&ndash;5 members.</li>\n<li>Team members must belong to the same institute.</li>\n<li>Inter-department and inter-specialization teams are allowed.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Competition Structure:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Round 0: Online Abstract Submission</strong></li>\n<li><strong style=\"color: #000000;\">Round 1: Online Software Simulation</strong></li>\n<li><strong style=\"color: #000000;\">Round 2: On-site Hardware Implementation, Live Demonstration, and Final Presentation</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Tracks:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>FPGA</li>\n<li>Raspberry Pi / Renesas Kit</li>\n<li>ESP32 / Arduino</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Problem Domains:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Communication Systems</li>\n<li>Biomedical Engineering</li>\n<li>Image and Signal Processing</li>\n<li>Processor Design</li>\n<li>Defence and Security</li>\n<li>Indian Knowledge Systems</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\" data-section-id=\"3sx7hp\" data-start=\"1312\" data-end=\"1342\">Team Details &amp; Registration</h2>\n<ul data-start=\"1343\" data-end=\"1837\">\n<li data-section-id=\"1hdsdxq\" data-start=\"1343\" data-end=\"1409\"><strong data-start=\"1345\" data-end=\"1359\">Team Size:</strong> Minimum <strong data-start=\"1368\" data-end=\"1373\">3</strong> and Maximum <strong data-start=\"1386\" data-end=\"1391\">5</strong> members per team.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"qj1bvo\" data-start=\"1410\" data-end=\"1491\"><strong data-start=\"1412\" data-end=\"1433\">Registration Fee:</strong> <strong data-start=\"1434\" data-end=\"1460\">₹1,200 per participant</strong> (<strong data-start=\"1462\" data-end=\"1489\">₹1,000 for IEEE Members</strong>).</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1tqt7k0\" data-start=\"1492\" data-end=\"1562\">The registration fee includes <strong data-start=\"1524\" data-end=\"1553\">food and registration kit</strong> charges.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"18j7jq2\" data-start=\"1563\" data-end=\"1628\"><strong data-start=\"1565\" data-end=\"1594\">Free hostel accommodation</strong> will be provided to participants.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"1nwd68m\" data-start=\"1629\" data-end=\"1661\"><strong data-start=\"1631\" data-end=\"1643\">No TA/DA</strong> will be provided.</li>\n<li data-section-id=\"4enegk\" data-start=\"1662\" data-end=\"1837\">Development boards will be provided by the organizers. Teams must bring their own <strong data-start=\"1746\" data-end=\"1809\">sensors, actuators, modules, and other required peripherals</strong> for project implementation.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Rules:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Projects must be original; plagiarism will lead to disqualification.</li>\n<li>Each team must select one official problem statement.</li>\n<li>Abstract submission is mandatory.</li>\n<li>The decision of the judges and organizing committee will be final and binding.</li>\n</ul>",
